p-FOLD RHOMBIC TILING (ODD PRIME p)
============================================================

MODULE:
  Λ = Z[ζ_p]  (cyclotomic module of rank p−1)
  ζ_p = exp(2πi/p)

SPLITTING:
  K = Q(ζ_p)  →  R^2  ⊕  R^(p−3)
  Physical embedding: σ_1(ζ_p) = exp(2πi/p)
  Internal embeddings: σ_j(ζ_p) = exp(2πij/p), j = 2..(p−1)/2

            High-Dimensional Cyclotomic Module: Λ = Z[ζ_p]
                                   │
              ┌────────────────────┴────────────────────┐
              │                                         │
              ▼                                         ▼
    Physical Projection (T_parallel)          Internal Projection (T_perp)
              │                                         │
              ▼                                         ▼
   Physical 2D Space (R^2)                  Window Space (R^{p-3})
   - Vertex positions                       - Multigrid offsets
   - Edge vectors Δx                        - Selection window filter


Space / Domain, Operator, Dynamics, Parameter Behavior
- Physical Space (R2), T_∥​, Expanding transformation, Scaled by λ=∣σ1​(β)∣>1
- Internal Space (Rp−3), T_⊥​, Contracting transformation, Scaled by matrix A⊥​ with ∣σj​(β)∣<1
- State Space (X=Λ×S×C), T_comb​, Combinatorial tile division, Driven by substitution matrix M

------------------------------------------------------------
T_parallel  :  Λ → R^2
------------------------------------------------------------
Definition:
  For x = Σ_{k=0}^{p−2} n_k ζ_p^k,

  T_parallel(x) =
      ( Σ_k n_k cos(2πk/p) ) * u1
    + ( Σ_k n_k sin(2πk/p) ) * u2

Interpretation:
  Physical-space placement of vertices.
  Rhomb edges = T_parallel(x2 − x1).

------------------------------------------------------------
T_perp  :  Λ → R^(p−3)
------------------------------------------------------------
Definition:
  For x = Σ_{k=0}^{p−2} n_k ζ_p^k,

  T_perp(x) =
    ( Σ_k n_k cos(4πk/p),
      Σ_k n_k cos(6πk/p),
      ...
      Σ_k n_k cos(2π((p−1)/2)k/p) )

Interpretation:
  Internal-space window coordinates.
  Multigrid offsets = translations in T_perp-space.

------------------------------------------------------------
T_comb  :  (Λ × S × C) → (Λ × S × C)
------------------------------------------------------------
State space:
  S = {1,2,...,(p−1)/2}   (rhomb shape index)
  C = combinatorial local configuration data
  X = Λ × S × C

Substitution matrix:
  M ∈ Z^{((p−1)/2) × ((p−1)/2)}
  Column m gives counts of rhomb types produced by inflating type m.

Action:
  T_comb(x, m, c) = { ( x_i , m_i , c_i ) }_{i=1..N_m }
  where:
    m_i determined by M_{m_i,m}
    x_i = β x + u_{m,i}
    β = Pisano unit in Z[ζ_p + ζ_p^{-1}]
    u_{m,i} ∈ Λ are displacement vectors

Interpretation:
  Pure combinatorial evolution under inflation.
  Tile types and adjacency rules encoded by M and u_{m,i}.

------------------------------------------------------------
INFLATION AUTOMORPHISM  T : Λ → Λ
------------------------------------------------------------
Definition:
  T(x) = β x
  β ∈ Z[ζ_p + ζ_p^{-1}] is a Pisano unit

Decomposition:
  Physical:   T_parallel(x) → λ * T_parallel(x)
              λ = |σ_1(β)| > 1

  Internal:   T_perp(x) → A_perp * T_perp(x)
              A_perp = matrix of β under embeddings σ_2..σ_{(p−1)/2}
              |σ_j(β)| < 1 for j ≥ 2

  Comb:       Tile types evolve via substitution matrix M

